    "description": "SPK Corporation, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the trading of automotive spare parts and accessories, and industrial vehicle parts in Japan, Asia, Oceania, Central America, South America, and internationally. The company offers engines, drivetrain, brakes, suspension, electrical, and air conditioning parts; and oil chemical products. It also supplies automotive aftermarket parts and accessories; and machinery equipment parts and components, including multifunction displays, integrated switches and dials, telematics equipment, electrical components such as lamps, resin parts, and functional parts to the manufacturers of construction vehicles, forklifts, and tractors. In addition, the company offers turbo charger, expander, liner and sleeve, valve stem seal, break master cylinder, caliper, oil jet check valve, drain cock, bush, piston pin, drive shaft, tool box, brake pad and shoe, brake disc rotor, battery, engine oil, torque rod bush, ignition coil, radiator, bulb, hose clamp, wiper, bead cream, brake lining rivet, LED work lamp, and CV joint. Further, it also provide engine parts such as fuel pump, throttle body, intake manifold, engine valve, timing chain, gasket, washer, oil seal, power steering seal, timing kit, engine bearing, bushing thrust washer, thermostat, and thermos sensor; drivetrain parts, such as propeller shaft, axle shaft, differencial, and universal joint; oil and chemicals, includes brake fluid and coolant; brake and suspension parts such as wheel cylinder, brake lining, control arm, oil pump, rubber bushing, shock absorber, ball joint, tie rod end, rack end, stabilizer link, control cables, hub bolt, U bolt, rubber bushing, center bearing, and engine mounting; and electrical and air conditioning parts. The company was formerly known as Daido Automobile Enterprising Co., Ltd. and changed its name to SPK Corporation in 1992. SPK Corporation was incorporated in 1917 and is headquartered in Osaka, Japan."
